// pendulum_dyn — a real pendulum: no drive at all, just a rod, a pin and
// gravity. Released from 60 degrees, it swings with its natural period
// T = 2*pi*sqrt(2L/(3g)) (a compound rod pendulum: the mass is spread along
// the rod, not lumped at the tip). The window title shows the live energy,
// which stays flat — that is the integrator's conservation guarantee.
//
//   mech run examples/pendulum_dyn.mech
//
mechanism pendulum_dyn {
  world { gravity: 9.81 }
  ground frame { anchor pivot at (0, 0) }
  rod arm { length: 1.0, from: 60 deg } on frame.pivot
}
